# gitleaks baseline — the fingerprints of findings that existed before the gate did.
#
# This file is what makes the rule stated at the top of .github/workflows/security.yml true: **fail
# on something new, never on the backlog**. A fingerprint is `commit:path:rule:line`, so an entry
# here suppresses one reviewed occurrence and nothing else — the same credential reintroduced in a
# new commit produces a new fingerprint and still breaks the build.
#
# Anything added here needs a reason on the line above it. "It was already failing" is not one.

